@id n5_choirc
# DRAFT
# Brother Piers on the east walk at dusk (night 5, clear and cold), looking at the chapter house door. Background; dry.
# What the brothers say now (and what some say quietly), and whether he'll leave: he has nowhere to go.
== start
(Brother Piers on the east walk, his breath smoking in the cold. He's looking at the chapter house door.)
Piers {grave}: Clear tonight. You can see every star. I'd sooner have the fog back.
-> topics

== again
Piers {calm}: Still cold.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n5_choirc_talk] What are the brothers saying? -> talk
* [if not n5_choirc_leave] Will you leave the abbey, brother? -> go

== talk [set n5_choirc_talk]
Piers {grave}: That it took the boy first because he was the youngest. That it walks in the fog. That it's no demon at all.
(He looks at you.)
Piers {wary}: Nobody says that last one loudly.
-> topics

== go [set n5_choirc_leave]
Piers {sad}: And go where? I've been in this house since I was nine. Outside that gate I'm a shaved head and no trade.
Piers {weary}: I'll stay. I'll keep a candle lit.
-> topics

== leave
Piers {calm}: Keep warm, porter.
